From 9176b6cca46f8e0ce3c027532b1f16a2c928e735 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Wed, 15 Apr 2026 17:39:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] gluon-status-page-mesh-batman-adv: show only the active
 algorithm's metric column
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A given Gluon build runs exactly one batman-adv routing algorithm
(mesh.batman_adv.routing_algo in site config). Showing both TQ and TP
columns on the status page always leaves one permanently blank and
confuses users. Emit only the relevant attr tuple:

- BATMAN_V → TP (throughput)
- BATMAN_IV → TQ (link quality)

The value is read from gluon.site at render time (mesh.lua is loaded
fresh per request), so it tracks the authoritative site config that
also drives gluon_bat0.sh and the kernel. check_site already
guarantees the field is one of {'BATMAN_IV', 'BATMAN_V'}.

No JS or HTML template change: status-page.html iterates mesh.attrs
dynamically, and the minified JS builds per-key cells from the
rendered <th data-key="..."> headers, so shrinking the list works
transparently. The Monitoring panel's separate "Gateway (TQ: ...)"
line is unrelated (batman-adv reports gateway TQ for both algos) and
stays unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../luasrc/lib/gluon/status-page/mesh.lua      | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/package/gluon-status-page-mesh-batman-adv/luasrc/lib/gluon/status-page/mesh.lua b/package/gluon-status-page-mesh-batman-adv/luasrc/lib/gluon/status-page/mesh.lua
index 010371c8..4795891b 100644
--- a/package/gluon-status-page-mesh-batman-adv/luasrc/lib/gluon/status-page/mesh.lua
+++ b/package/gluon-status-page-mesh-batman-adv/luasrc/lib/gluon/status-page/mesh.lua
@@ -1,3 +1,16 @@
+local site = require 'gluon.site'
+
+local attrs
+if site.mesh.batman_adv.routing_algo() == 'BATMAN_V' then
+	attrs = {
+		{'tp', 'Throughput', 'bit/s', 'bitrate'},
+	}
+else
+	attrs = {
+		{'tq', 'TQ', ' %'},
+	}
+end
+
 return {
 	provider = '/cgi-bin/dyn/neighbours-batadv',
 	-- List of mesh-specific attributes, each a tuple of
@@ -5,8 +18,5 @@ return {
 	-- 2) human-readable key (not translatable yet)
 	-- 3) value suffix (optional)
 	-- 4) formatter name (optional) -- key into status-page.js formats{}
-	attrs = {
-		{'tq', 'TQ', ' %'},
-		{'tp', 'Throughput', 'bit/s', 'bitrate'},
-	},
+	attrs = attrs,
 }
